A converter declared peak alone = 6.900000 A; onset margin +0.195710 (+2.76%); no per-lead peak apportioned by A.

Held A peak 6.900 = B peak 6.000 + wall peak 0.900 + D8 ZERO. D8 and wall are not outlets dropped by D-11.

POWER-THERMAL.md:706-711,1037-1038 PS-ALLTX PLAN/HIGH = 5.89/7.8 A at converter. HIGH onset margin -0.704290 (-9.93%); HIGH is inside the loop band, not below it. PWR-F01 to PWR-F03 at lines 960-962 also flag understated child declarations.

Recommend SESSION decision: converter peak 8.900 A coincident BOUND; 7.900 A with D8 typical. Limiter: LM5176 average-loop fold-back (SNVSAI1D p.17), reducing output voltage if sustained demand reaches its threshold. Device brown-out/shared-fabric loss is possible; REQ-018 regulation remains unproven. Draft applies only interim typical alignment, not this pending peak decision.

